isions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, keeps calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology. Candidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nWe need to discuss criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nAgent 1 argued C is best due to reliability and decision quality, despite communication issues.\n\nWe could either agree or challenge. Let's see if any other candidate may be stronger overall.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but weak memory for numbers (attention), makes nasty remarks (crew cooperation, communication). So B has strong reliability and stress resilience, but crew cooperation is a serious concern (makes nasty remarks). That could be a safety risk.\n\nCandidate D: takes responsibility seriously (reliability), solves problems extremely well (decision quality), can concentrate (attention), responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), but has hot temper (crew cooperation, communication), and is a know-it-all (cooperation). So D has strong technical and decision, but cooperation issues.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates dangerous situations (decision quality), sees complex connections (technical), excellent spatial vision (technical), very good leadership (crew cooperation), but regarded as show-off (crew cooperation), not open to new ideas (adaptability). No explicit stress resilience or reliability info. Might be less reliable.\n\nThus C still seems strongest overall: reliability 100%, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere, calm in crisis, understands technology. Communication issues exist but maybe less severe than B's nasty remarks or D's hot temper. So we may agree with Agent 1.\n\nWe should provide our own evidence: C is 100% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Also note concerns: difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education. Then argue that despite these, his reliability and decision quality outweigh, and his calmness in crisis adds stress resilience, making him best.\n\nThus we vote Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's point. Provide our own facts.\n\nLet's craft PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I concur with Agent 1's recommendation of Candidate C because ...\". Provide evidence.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
